A||N||8||TONY_C||1988 Fiero Strut measurements, need help||||1||
Z||000000||TONY_C||06-14-2001||11:44 AM||||I'm wondering if I can get some assistance from one of you '88 owners out there. I need two simple measurements for the mounting studs on the strut towers from an 88 Fiero. There are three studs on each strut which mount the strut to the strut tower. I need the center to center distance between the innermost stud on each tower, that is the distance from the center of the inboard stud on the left tower to the center of the inboard stud on the right tower. I also need the distance from the center of this stud to the rear windshield. I am doing some work to an 84 which involves using the 88 subframe and these dimensions are not the same for the 88 model year. I know in the 84 shop manual under the body section there are the dimensions for these bolts, maybe one of you 88 owners has an 88 shop manual or would be kind enough to measure them directly off your Fiero. Thanks for the assistance. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Toddster||06-14-2001||12:04 PM||||37 5/16 inches from center to center and 17 inches exactly from center to the metal substructure behind the rear window (16 1/2 inches to the glass itself).||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||06-14-2001||12:36 PM||||Tony,<P>Don't know it this will be useful or not, but Held Motorsports <A HREF="http://www.heldmotorsports.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.heldmotorsports.com</A>  <BR>sells adapter plates for the installation of an 88 cradle into an earlier car. It requires the use of coil-overs, though.<P>Welcome aboard!<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"||||reg||1
Z||000003||TONY_C||06-14-2001||01:02 PM||||Toddster,<BR>thanks for the quick reply. Just to make sure, the dimensions you gace me are form the mounting stud and not from the big nut on the center of the strut, right?<P>Thanks again to those who responded,<BR>Tony||||reg||1
Z||000004||Will||06-14-2001||01:10 PM||||The '88 manual has those dimensions. I don't has access to it right now, but if you can wait until saturday, I can give you the specs from the manual.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Toddster||06-14-2001||03:36 PM||||sorry Tony_c, I gave you the measurement from the center lug. <P>The measurement from the mounting bolts is 33 3/8 inches for the inner most bolts.<P>I just measured it to make sure. This measurement is the official Datum line from PO-3 of the KLM Guide.<P>I can give other measurements as needed.||||reg||1
Z||000006||WampusCat||06-14-2001||04:37 PM||||The manual has the measurement from the strut bolt holes towards the front of the car, but I can't find one for the bolts that are closest to each other.  From center to center on the forward attaching bolt is 40.5"||||reg||1
Z||000007||TONY_C||06-15-2001||07:59 AM||||Toddster,<BR>thanks for the info and the correction. did you take the original measurement of 16.5" to the rear glass from the center lug or is that the distance from the center of the innermost strut mounting bolt?  Again, thanks for your help.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Toddster||06-15-2001||12:29 PM||||The glass measurement is the same since the center lug and the inner bolts are on the same centerline. Good luck.||||reg||1
